>     What's partial autocorrelation?
 > McKay can give a better answer, but generally, http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Partial_autocorrelation_function

OK.  We probably don't need to plot this (though the
order of an AR model is calculated via DIC by the
Coda effective sample size calcuation -- so it's not
that far out).

> Right now, it displays just one chain; the default is to use the first chain. I can imagine a single plot that displays
> all chains, differentiating by color just as the other plots do.

