This is already there, see enclosed and ?mcmcplots::traplot.

> I propose doing exactly zero hypothesis tests.

I don't want to do hypothesis tests, but it seems handy to flag huge
convergence problems if we can. Would it be sensible to do a
rule-of-thumb test instead? Say, if chains have very different
autocorrelation, or if R-hat or n.eff suggest that there are problems.

