adaptation.  These should NOT be used as samples.

I completely agree it's better for mcmcplots not to depend
on our Rcpp wrapped mcmc::chains object.  It'll be
a maintenance/install nightmare you don't need.

We don't need anything special for parameter scatterplots.
It was just meant as an example of the kinds of things we
look at.  As long as the data's there, we can do all sorts
of things like traceplots as "regular old plots with MCMC data".
I'm not sure where the package should draw the line.

Personally, once I verified that R-hats were OK, I only ever
used the data out of R2WinBUGS.

- Bob

