I too have long thought that the FSF licenses are much easier to understand with compiled code than with functional code. If RStan were only R code, then it certainly could be BSD. But if the C++ in RStan links to Rcpp's GPL'd headers, then it is a derivative work. Possibly, there is some hybrid where the C++ code in RStan could be GPL while the R code could be BSD but I don't know and I doubt if it is worth pursuing.

> >     I've never understood these "GPL vX or later" things.
> >     Why would anyone agree to license their software under
> >     a license that doesn't exist yet?  Or am I misreading
