RE:P.P.S.: I think Radford's assuming that you're holding εL fixed,
and varying ε and L as necessary to ensure a reasonable acceptance
rate. So cost is proportional to 1/ε, and 1/ε has to grow as d^1/4, so
cost grows as d^5/4.

