What happens when we have Bernoulli with prob > 1?  Does it just set the density to 0?
Regarding the dogs example:  I actually know all about this one, as it's in my book (assuming it's the same dogs example that I know about).  The parameters are supposed to be restricted so that both alpha and beta are negative.  Also, the model is set up so that xa and xs are always nonnegative.  If you actually send in negative values for xa or xs, or positive values for alpha or beta, than I have no idea what will happen.
A

