It's one of my favorite examples.  I had no idea it made its way into Bugs.  It's from an experiment from about 1950 and the data were originally analyzed by Fred Mosteller, who I was a TA for in his last semester teaching at Harvard.  It was also an early example of simulation-based model checking (from 1954), Mosteller compared real dogs to "stat-dogs."

